# Skill: browse

## Overview

This skill drives a real browser through Aside to open pages, read content, click through flows, take screenshots, and check console errors. It's part of the gstack toolkit for web automation and testing.

## Capabilities

- **Page Navigation**: Open and navigate to web pages
- **Content Reading**: Extract and read page content
- **Interaction**: Click through flows and interact with page elements
- **Screenshot Capture**: Take screenshots of pages
- **Console Error Checking**: Monitor and report browser console errors
- **Session Management**: Manage browser sessions
- **Real Browser**: Uses a real browser instance (not headless)

## Use Cases

### Testing
- Test web application flows
- Verify user journeys
- Capture visual evidence

### Development
- Debug web applications
- Test responsive design
- Validate UI behavior

### Automation
- Automate repetitive web tasks
- Extract data from web pages
- Create automated workflows

## Example Usage

```
opencode run "Use browse to open https://example.com and take a screenshot"

opencode run "Use browse to click through the checkout flow on the e-commerce site"

opencode run "Use browse to check for console errors on the production site"
```

## Technical Details

This skill uses the Aside browser automation framework to drive a real browser instance. It provides full browser control and real-time interaction capabilities.

## Output

The skill provides:
- Page content
- Screenshots
- Console errors
- Navigation history
- Interaction results

